AD  - K.S. Rangasamy College of Technology, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Namakkal, India
AB  - Semantic segmentation architectures are good in classification and localization of object boundaries in images. Four different architectures are chosen for segmentation and classification of diseased portion in turmeric crop. Quadrature Discriminant Feature Selection (QDFS) is implemented in one of the convolutional layers in all the architectures. This estimates an individual covariance matrix for every class and models non-linear relationships. The turmeric data set is huge and the feature set taken for classification is very large which increases the complexity of the networks. QDFS chooses the relevant features and eliminates the additional features. The results of classification are evaluated with metrics such as validation accuracy, Intersection over union, validation loss and dice coefficient. FCN8, PSP Net, Deep Lab V3 and MobileNetV3 (small) are the four architectures taken for comparative analysis. Real time dataset of about 4000 images is collected for the analysis. The observed results show that mobile Net v3 small has the highest validation accuracy and lowest validation loss with good intersection over union and Dice coefficient values. © 2022 IEEE.
