AB  - Egocentric hand segmentation is crucial for natural interaction in AR/VR systems, but existing methods often struggle to balance accuracy and real-time efficiency on edge devices. While SAM-based models offer strong generalization capabilities, their computationally intensive decoders hinder practical deployment. To address this challenge, we propose SegLite Decoder (SLDC), a lightweight, prompt-free decoder tailored for efficient SAM variants such as MobileSAM and EdgeSAM. In SLDC, depthwise separable convolutions and a novel ConvSE block are introduced to enhance fine-grained hand feature representation with minimal computational overhead. Additionally, a composite training loss, combining multi-scale supervision with Sobel-based boundary refinement, improves edge quality without increasing inference costs. Experimental results show that EdgeSAM+SLDC achieves the high real-time performance at 71.37 FPS with a batch size of 1, highlighting its efficiency for latency-sensitive AR/VR applications. © 2026 IEEE.
