AD  - SMU MedTech, Tunis, Tunisia
AB  - Vision Transformers (ViTs) excel at semantic segmentation but face critical deployment challenges on resource-constrained edge devices. While models like SegFormer and TopFormer have made strides in efficiency, they often rely on static token processing that wastes computational resources on redundant image regions. We introduce AdaViT-Edge, an adaptive architecture achieving real-Time semantic segmentation through three synergistic innovations: (1) A Dynamic Token Router (DTR) that intelligently prunes up to 68% of redundant tokens using spatial entropy and attention uncertainty, (2) A Hierarchical Attention Compression (HAC) mechanism that adaptively adjusts attention resolution across network depth, and (3) A Mixed-Precision Quantization strategy guided by layer-wise sensitivity analysis. AdaViT-Edge achieves 74.2% mIoU on Cityscapes with only 2.8 GFLOPs, running at 28 FPS on a Raspberry Pi 5-representing a 3.2× speedup over existing efficient ViT methods. This work bridges the gap between transformer accuracy and edge efficiency, enabling real-Time vision applications in autonomous vehicles, mobile robotics, and IoT systems.  © 2026 IEEE.
