AB  - Modern agriculture is changing due to recent developments in the field of artificial intelligence and machine learning. The review pools the most recent trends in ML approaches in the various areas of agricultural problem solving, with a focus on crop recommendation, yield prediction, disease and weed detection, resource management and chaining of IoT and remote sensing technologies. The review is based on the more than 20-plus studies of high-impact studies and suggests a new area of investigation that is based on scalable AI solutions to support multi-crop, multi-region agricultural settings. The literature synthesis is an example of domain breakthroughs and ongoing gaps in research, which leads to a roadmap to smart, sustainable agriculture in the future.  © 2026 IEEE.
