AD  - St. Joseph's College Of Engineering, Department Of Information Technology, Chennai, India
AB  - Deploying deep neural networks on resource-constrained edge devices requires hardware-aware adaptive compression. We introduce a multi-objective hardware-in-the-loop framework that optimizes accuracy, latency, energy, and memory jointly through: (i) hardware-specific cost-model-guided adaptive multi-granularity pruning, (ii) hierarchical knowledge distillation with latency-energy regularization, and (iii) energy-cognizant dynamic early-exit mechanisms with reinforcement learning-driven optimization. Our framework is verified on the Raspberry Pi 4 using ResNet-18 and MobileNetV2 on CIFAR-10/100, achieving up to 48.3 % latency reduction, 42.7 % memory savings, and 42.0% energy reduction at only 0.9 % accuracy degradation. Our reinforcement learning-driven optimized exit policy achieves 1.93 × speedup at an accuracy of 92.2 %.: © 2026 IEEE.
